<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: right"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><IMG SRC="tm2628346d1_ex99-1img01.jpg" ALT=""></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>Ribbon Communications Inc. Reports<BR>
Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>Revenue increased 14% sequentially and Net
Income improved by $18M;</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>further significant gains expected in 4Q 2026</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>IP Optical Networks Revenue increased 17% QoQ
led by new wins in North America</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>Cloud and Edge Revenue increased 11% QoQ led
by U.S. Tier 1 Network Modernization</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>Growing Pipeline of Data Center and AI-related
Opportunities</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>PLANO, Texas &ndash; </B><U>Ribbon Communications Inc.</U> (Nasdaq:
RBBN), a global leader in real-time communications technology,&nbsp;IP routing, and optical networking solutions, today announced its
financial results for the third quarter of 2026.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Third Quarter 2026 Highlights</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Financial
Results</B></FONT><B>&sup1;:</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in">&nbsp;</TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Revenue
                                            was $219 million, compared to $215 million for the third quarter of 2025</FONT></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in">&nbsp;</TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">GAAP
                                            Operating Income was $6 million, compared to $3 million for the third quarter of 2025</FONT></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in">&nbsp;</TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Non-GAAP
                                            Adjusted EBITDA was $27 million, compared to $29 million for the third quarter of 2025</FONT></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in">&nbsp;</TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">GAAP
                                            Gross Margin was 48.2%, compared to 50.1% for the third quarter of 2025</FONT></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in">&nbsp;</TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.25in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Non-GAAP
                                            Gross Margin was 50.3%, compared to 52.6% for the third quarter of 2025</FONT></TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&ldquo;We had meaningful sequential increases in revenue and
profitability in both of our operating segments again in the third quarter, consistent with our second quarter results commentary.
The strong IP Optical Networks bookings trend in the first half of the year translated into a record third quarter sales for the
business, growing 5% year over year and included two new U.S. Tier 2 Internet Service Provider customers,&rdquo; stated Bruce
McClelland, President and Chief Executive Officer of Ribbon Communications. &ldquo;We are also encouraged by increased activity in
the Cloud and Edge segment with Service Provider revenue growing 15% sequentially supported by a 50% increase in sales to our
largest customer, along with further growth in the Enterprise and Government market segments. This progress clearly supports the
second-half improvement we expected, with positive trends in both operating segments and stronger results projected for the fourth
quarter. Looking ahead to 2027, we see further growth drivers with the adoption of voice-enabled Enterprise AI applications, new
solutions to mitigate AI-generated voice-phishing cyber-attacks, and broader demand for data center fiber infrastructure.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">Rick Marmurek, Chief Financial Officer of Ribbon Communications, remarked,
&ldquo;Our performance improved significantly in the third quarter, with revenue increasing 14% and Adjusted EBITDA more than doubling
to $27 million from $12 million in the second quarter. At the same time, Non-GAAP operating expenses remained at $88 million. We continue
to focus on expanding margins, maintaining strong cost discipline, and further strengthening our balance sheet.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

